# Add New Calculator

When the user asks to add a new calculator, follow this workflow:

## Input

The user provides a calculator topic (e.g. "auto loan calculator", "inflation calculator").

## Step 1: Register in Data

Add the calculator entry to `src/lib/calculators.ts`:

```typescript
{
  slug: "the-slug",
  title: "Full Calculator Title",
  shortTitle: "Short Name",
  description: "One sentence description (50-160 chars) targeting the main search keyword.",
  category: "loans" | "savings" | "debt" | "planning",
}
```

Add a corresponding SVG icon to `src/components/Icons.tsx` in the `iconMap`.

## Step 2: Create Calculator Directory

Create `src/app/calculators/[slug]/` with three files:

### page.tsx (route entry)

```typescript
import type { Metadata } from "next";
import { getCalculator } from "@/lib/calculators";
import { site } from "@/lib/site";
import { CalculatorShell } from "@/components/CalculatorShell";
import { [Name]Calculator } from "./[Name]Calculator";
import { [Name]Article } from "./[Name]Article";

const calc = getCalculator("[slug]")!;

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: calc.title,
  description: calc.description,
  openGraph: { title: `${calc.title} | ${site.name}`, description: calc.description, type: "website" },
};

export default function [Name]Page() {
  return (
    <CalculatorShell calculator={calc} article={<[Name]Article />}>
      <[Name]Calculator />
    </CalculatorShell>
  );
}
```

### [Name]Calculator.tsx (interactive widget)

- Must be a `"use client"` component
- Use `InputField` component from `@/components/InputField`
- All calculation logic in a `useMemo` hook
- Format currency with `toLocaleString("en-US", { style: "currency", currency: "USD" })`
- Show results in colored cards (bg-brand-50, bg-accent-50, bg-ink-100)
- Include data tables or breakdowns where applicable
- NO emoji anywhere

### [Name]Article.tsx (educational content)

- Must contain 800-1200 words minimum
- Structure: How it works → Key concepts → Practical examples → Tips → FAQ (3-5 questions)
- Include at least one infographic image generated with kie-image skill:

```bash
node ~/.cursor/skills/kie-image/generate.mjs "[descriptive prompt for infographic]" "3:2" --resolution 2K
```

Download to `public/images/[slug]-[description].png` and embed with:

```tsx
import Image from "next/image";

<figure className="my-8">
  <Image
    src="/images/[slug]-[description].png"
    alt="Descriptive alt text for SEO"
    width={1024}
    height={683}
    className="rounded-lg border border-ink-200"
  />
  <figcaption className="mt-2 text-center text-sm text-ink-500">
    Caption explaining the visual.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
```

Content requirements:
- Add unique perspective: specific dollar-amount examples, comparison tables, scenario analysis
- Include at least one concrete "case study" example (e.g. "Sarah earns $75,000/year and wants to...")
- Add a comparison table where relevant (e.g. 15yr vs 30yr, different rates)
- NO generic filler — every paragraph must provide actionable insight
- NO emoji anywhere

## Step 3: Update Sitemap

The sitemap auto-generates from `calculators` array — no manual update needed.

## Step 4: Verify

Run `npm run build` and confirm the new page appears in the route list.

## Step 5: Commit

```bash
git add -A && git commit -m "Add [calculator name] calculator"
```

## Quality Checklist

- [ ] Calculator logic uses correct financial formula
- [ ] All inputs have sensible defaults
- [ ] Results update reactively as user types
- [ ] Article has 800+ words with unique examples
- [ ] At least 1 infographic image generated and embedded
- [ ] No emoji used anywhere
- [ ] SVG icon added to Icons.tsx iconMap
- [ ] Build passes with no errors
